13. Data & Privacy Principles
The V1.0 release-completeness work must preserve REELHOUSE's local-first philosophy.
The application must not require:
- user accounts
- cloud library accounts
- online authentication for basic application use
- cloud storage for the library
- social profiles
Export must not silently expose:
- TMDB credentials
- private credentials
- unrelated device information
Feedback must not automatically expose:
- media files
- personal files
- private library contents
- API credentials
14. Implementation Strategy
Each milestone should be implemented as a bounded engineering task.
Recommended sequence:
RC.1
Library Export / Import
        ↓
RC.2
First-Run Onboarding
        ↓
RC.3
TMDB Setup Experience
        ↓
RC.4
Feedback & Suggestions
        ↓
RC.5
About & Credits
        ↓
RC.6
Launch Experience
        ↓
RC.7
Update Checking
        ↓
FINAL FEATURE FREEZE
This sequence intentionally handles the architecturally significant pieces first.
Each milestone should be implemented and verified independently before moving to the next.
15. Acceptance Standard
A milestone is not considered complete merely because the UI exists.
Each RC milestone requires:
Functional Correctness
The feature works through its complete user flow.
Persistence
Relevant state survives application restart.
Error Handling
Expected failure conditions have understandable UI responses.
Offline / Local Behavior
The feature does not accidentally violate REELHOUSE's local-first architecture.
Regression Safety
Existing library, playback, collection and offline-media behavior remains intact.
Automated Verification
Appropriate tests are added for new logic and important edge cases.
Manual Verification
The actual user flow is tested in the target application.
16. Final Feature Freeze
After RC.1–RC.7 are accepted:
REELHOUSE V1.0 enters FINAL FEATURE FREEZE.

No additional user-facing functionality should be added to V1.0.
At that point, the project moves exclusively into:
Production Readiness
- fresh-install testing
- migration testing
- real-library testing
- performance testing
- reliability testing
- packaging
- signing
- release configuration
- update mechanism verification
- backup/restore verification
- platform-specific testing
- security/privacy review
- final regression testing
Then:
Production Readiness
        ↓
Release Candidate
        ↓
Final Regression
        ↓
REELHOUSE v1.0
17. V1.0 Completion Definition
REELHOUSE V1.0 is considered release-complete when a new user can:
Install REELHOUSE → experience the launch → create their local profile → configure TMDB or skip it knowingly → create/import their library → use their cinema → report a problem → receive a future release notification → understand what was fixed → update the application.

And an existing user can:
Export their library → install REELHOUSE elsewhere → import it → reconnect their physical media → continue using their collection.

That is the complete V1.0 lifecycle.
